{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1172662-gorgon-bloodline-update-2e","id":1172662,"title":"Gorgon Bloodline Update [2E]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-02T09:23:48-08:00","id":1172662,"title":"Gorgon Bloodline Update [2E]","content":"I've been working on a rough revision of the Gorgon Bloodline to fall in line with the thematic nature of Requiem 2E. I haven't quite finished all the rules stuff but I felt like the Bloodline needed to incorporate each of the Ventrue disciplines, especially dominate.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Animalism, Dominate, Protean, Resilience <br /> <br /> <br /> Weakness:<br /> <br /> Unlike their Ventrue cousins, Gorgons also experience a dependence on \u2014 and an unbreakable link to \u2014 the legendry from which they claim their power. Without a serpent in contact with her person, a Medusa suffers a \u20133 penalty on all Discipline dice pools and may not spend Vitae to augment Physical dice pools. Additionally, Protean may be only used to gain snake-like features.<br /> <br /> DEVOTIONS: (3xp Each)<br /> <br /> Gorgon's Servant (Automatic upon joining the Bloodline):<br /> <br /> Gain a specialty in &quot;Snakes&quot; that applies to all skills. Let's a Gorgon directly control, sense and act through any snake which is in physical contact with their body. Additionally, a Gorgon may swallow a snake and for 1 vitae regurgitate similar snakes up to their BP. The Gorgon may not control more snakes than their BP [or maybe (1/2 BP) + 1 rounded up].<br /> <br /> Eye of Medusa (Prerequisite: Dominate 2)<br /> <br /> The Gorgon may freeze any target in place by staring into their eyes. Most notably this power may also be used through the snakes created by Gorgon's servants. This power does not have any cost, but the gaze must be maintained and the target may roll a contested Resolve + BP to resist against Gorgons Intelligence + Expression + Dominate. If they fail, and are attacked, they may roll again each turn.<br /> <br /> Scales of the Serpent (Prerequisite: Resilience 2)<br /> For 2 BP, the Kindred may gain amor = Resilience for the remainder of the scene. This armor manifests as hard scales that form on the Gorgon's skin. <br /> <br /> Medusa's Venom (Prerequisite: Protean 2, Resilience 1)<br /> Convert vitae into venom: apply to weapon, or inflict by bite; basic: paralytic venom; with experience, Lethal venom.<br /> <br /> Body of the Gorgon (Prerequisite: Protean 3)<br /> Convert legs into snake tail. Size 6. Speed 8. May spit venom. May reflexively use dominate on any character effected by Eye of Medusa. <br /> <br /> Any input would be appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T10:15:47-08:00","id":1172676,"title":"","content":"This is a kind of short and rather mechanical write-up. And, well, without being an expert on the mechanics of 2nd edition, I think it looks kind of good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T08:00:43-08:00","id":1174279,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't force the fact that a Gorgon would only adopt reptilian Protean powers, it doesn't have to be a weakness, it simply makes sense that they won't adopt any other form.<br /> <br /> Everything else looks okay, though I'm getting Setite flashbacks from this lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T09:19:38-08:00","id":1174295,"title":"","content":"Kinda seems like they should have a Nightmare + Protean power to actually turn targets to stone (based on Mortal Terror). But that doesn't fit their Discipline spread. I wonder if it would work with a Nosferatu variant...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}